Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 14:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] goodix550c: cover the pad with more enrollment samples

Enrollment keeps one independent SIGFM template per sample and verification
takes the best score across them, with no alignment or stitching. Matching
therefore requires the verifying touch to overlap an enrolled position, and on
this 108x88 pad eight positions do not cover it.

Measured on the same finger. A session placed consistently scored 2508, 3609,
264 and 2232 on four samples and 0 on the other four, matching easily. A
session where the operator deliberately spread the eight placements, which is
what every other reader invites, scored 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0 and did not
match its own finger at all.

Raise the sample count so ordinary varied placement still lands on an enrolled
position. The score gate is untouched: an overlapping touch clears it more
than twentyfold, so the shortfall is coverage rather than sensitivity, and
lowering the gate instead would buy tolerance by accepting weaker evidence.

Each added sample costs the operator one placement at enrollment.

---

--- a/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-private.h
+++ b/drivers/goodix53x5/goodix53x5-private.h
@@ -57,8 +57,21 @@
 /* FDT base length */
 #define GOODIX_FDT_BASE_LEN 24
 
-/* Enroll stages */
-#define GOODIX_ENROLL_SAMPLES 8
+/* Enroll stages.
+ *
+ * Enrollment keeps one independent SIGFM template per sample and verification
+ * takes the best score across them, with no alignment or stitching between
+ * samples. Matching therefore needs the verifying touch to overlap one enrolled
+ * position, and on a 108x88 pad eight positions do not cover it: an operator who
+ * deliberately spread eight placements, as every other reader invites, scored 0
+ * against all eight, while a session placed consistently scored 2508, 3609, 264
+ * and 2232 on four of them and 0 on the other four.
+ *
+ * The gate below is not the problem — an overlapping touch clears it more than
+ * twentyfold — so this raises coverage rather than lowering sensitivity. Each
+ * added sample costs the operator one placement.
+ */
+#define GOODIX_ENROLL_SAMPLES 16
 
 /* SIGFM (SIFT-based) matching parameters.
  * This gate is tuned for TX-off p3 preprocessing plus mutual SIGFM matching;

